  "answer": "In Q1 2026, citation reliability was the single most prominent customer complaint [NL-010#NL-010-S01]. An audit of 210 accuracy-related tickets found the issues were incorrect file links (42%), missing page numbers (28%), empty citations (18%), and broken links (12%) [NL-010#NL-010-S05]. These inaccuracies caused safety and trust problems, such as BrightPath Healthcare pausing its clinical pilot and Northstar Financial losing confidence in citations [NL-010#NL-010-S05].\n\nIn Q2 2026, the trend reversed after the April 2026 release. Citation accuracy tickets fell from 88 in March to 42 in April, 31 in May, and 24 in June [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. Citation-related complaints decreased significantly [NL-016#NL-016-S04], the overall NPS rose from 41 to 44 largely because of the April fix [NL-011#NL-011-S01], and customers reported that citations now direct them to the exact section or page range in source documents [NL-011#NL-011-S03]. Residual issues remained for scanned, image-only PDFs and temporary citation lag during peak hours [NL-011#NL-011-S05], with OCR limitations still a pain point for healthcare and manufacturing customers [NL-016#NL-016-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
